From: OpenImprenta spike <noreply@openimprenta.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Do not abort the whole import when the OLE metadata is broken

MSPUBParser::parse() calls parseMetaData() with the comment "No check:
metadata are not important enough to fail if they can't be parsed", but an
EndOfStreamException thrown while reading \005SummaryInformation or
\005DocumentSummaryInformation escapes parse() and the document is rejected
(MSPUBDocument::parse() catches it and returns false).

Seen on Apache POI's SampleBrochure.pub and SampleNewsletter.pub: both fail
with "Something bad happened here! Tell: 152" and no page is produced.

--- a/src/lib/MSPUBParser.cpp
+++ b/src/lib/MSPUBParser.cpp
@@ -188,7 +188,15 @@ bool MSPUBParser::parse()
   if (!m_input->isStructured())
     return false;
   // No check: metadata are not important enough to fail if they can't be parsed
-  parseMetaData();
+  try
+  {
+    parseMetaData();
+  }
+  catch (...)
+  {
+    MSPUB_DEBUG_MSG(("Couldn't parse metadata, ignoring.\n"));
+    m_input->seek(0, librevenge::RVNG_SEEK_SET);
+  }
   std::unique_ptr<librevenge::RVNGInputStream> quill(m_input->getSubStreamByName("Quill/QuillSub/CONTENTS"));
   if (!quill)
   {
